  <prompt>
    Build the dispatchUncertain routing-confidence producer that feeds the Confirm When Uncertain tier: low-confidence dispatch triggers the gate; high-confidence does not. The signal derives from the existing single agent turn's routing confidence — NOT a new classifier/scorer.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior .NET developer expert in the SPAARKE dispatch spine and ADR-039 (one probabilistic decider).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A dispatchUncertain signal derived from the existing dispatch decision is available to the gate. Low-confidence dispatch fires the Confirm When Uncertain gate; high-confidence does not. Covered by tests/integration/seam/** + unit tests. No second intent mechanism introduced.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Completes the risk-gate wiring: 021 handles explicit sprk_risk tiers; this handles the confidence-driven tier. The confidence must come from the one decider, preserving ADR-039.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/Gate/</file>
      <file>tests/integration/seam/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">The confidence signal MUST derive from the single agent turn; MUST NOT introduce a second scorer/classifier/reranker.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-043">Dispatch-spine change → tests/integration/seam/** DoD mandatory.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse the shipped dispatch seam; no new endpoint.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
